Myth: In the valley of Veilmere, a river wound between hills like a silver thread. The people tended not to gold but to promises, weaving them into a communal blanket that warmed every cottage. Each dawn, a gift passed—bread to a healer, a flute to a farmer, a story to a child. The blanket grew soft with kindness and stiff with fear when trust frayed, leaving cold corners where ice formed on doorframes.

