A trader named Carric, hungry for his own gain, tried to cloak a theft with empty apologies. The loom stuttered, a frost gliding along the riverbank. Yet the village gathered, offered extra returns, and rewove the damaged area with bright new threads of apology and shared toil. From then on, Veilmere prospered not by force, but by a living pledge—care returned, care multiplied, and the blanket of trust kept all hearts warm even in the harshest season.
